Function Requirement

  Feature requirement gathering follows two methods for a complex system
    USE CASE  - scenario in which a system is used
        identify users/actors for the system
        capture and describe all possible scenerios
    USER FLOW - Geographical representation of each use case
        expand use case through flow of events
        events contain : ACTION and DATA(to and from)

Unified Modeling Languege (UML) - Sequence diagram
   interaction between actors and objects
   standard for visualising system design
   Output of the sequence diagram provides API (eg HTTP verbs) calls details

Quality Attributes non-functional requirements
   provide a quality measure on how well the system performs on a particular dimension
   measurable and testable -  otherwise we wont know if they perform well or poorly
   Tradeoffs - no systems can provide all the quality attributes
   Feasibility - make sure the system is capable to deliver the requirement

